      "worked": "Since $y\\propto\\frac1x$, $xy=k$.\n$$\\begin{align*}k&=1\\times12\\\\k&=12\\end{align*}$$\nHence $y=\\frac{12}{x}$ and $x=\\frac{12}{y}$.\nWhen $x=2$, $y=\\frac{12}{2}=6$.\nWhen $y=4$, $x=\\frac{12}{4}=3$.\nWhen $x=4$, $y=\\frac{12}{4}=3$.\nWhen $y=24$, $x=\\frac{12}{24}=\\frac12$.",
